            "review_title": "Review at EL Doko Teppanyaki & Omakase",
            "review_text": "Erena A\nSydney, Australia6 contributions\n0\nA lively and delicious take on Japanese fine dining\nJun 2024 • Couples\nEL Doko offers a refreshing and exciting approach to Japanese cuisine, seamlessly blending the interactive fun of Teppanyaki with the curated experience of Omakase. Located on the bustling Dong Khoi street, this restaurant provides a surprisingly affordable fine-dining experience without compromising on quality.\nWhat sets EL Doko apart is its ability to cater to a wider audience. Those hesitant about the heavily raw-focused traditional Omakase will find comfort in the combined model, allowing them to enjoy cooked dishes alongside premium ingredients like A4 and A5 Wagyu beef.\nThe chefs, including the friendly Thai head chef Diow, are incredibly skilled and engaging, ensuring a lively atmosphere. The staff is attentive and sweet, adding to the overall positive experience. 👍\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten July 2, 2024",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
