            "review_text": "Ted Nguyen\nHouston, Texas7 contributions\n0\nExperiences not worth the money.\nFeb 2024 • Family\nThis spot is not any true foodies. It mostly for beginner to see show with out tasting.\n1. The ventilation is so terrible. Where each course is taste the same, for all I am smelling is the burning of the grease from both side of the grill. 2. The chef is using metal on caviar. When I ask him why. He have no clue that the metal chopstick he use will cause the caviar to oxidize and change its flavor. He also added. They store in tin can. This also tell me this chef have no clue that manufacturers place non-reactive interior linings in cans to prevent any adverse effects in all the tin. 3. This tell me the head chef of this place is a noobie. He may know how to cut and decor and copy ingredients, but he doesn't know about how each ingredient are to be. 4. One chef ask us on our next course of fried rice. She ask \"how much rice do we want? Full or less?\" . I am now convince this place is only good for the looks and entertainment. not a place to taste great food. Never in any tasting course a chef as how much you want. 5 The steak. So confusing on how to eat their style. it have 4 different combination of salt, sauce, and some other items... I am lost when chef tell me how to eat a nice steak make it boring. I simply just ate it as is with out follow those crazy instructions. the steak should taste of its own fine way. It's natural marble fat, the burnt from the grill. 6. Great food should be introduction to customer the right way. El Doko 11 Dong Khoi. Do have great service. How ever the chef are lack in knowledge and experience on tasting food. For certain. when it come to tasting of many course. Chef should understand, after each course. The palate taste buds must be clear to enjoy each course of its own natural tasting. All I am tasting was the same smell from the grill. 7. none of the chef have hair net or head wear. \nI finally lost and 